# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vendored upstream clones — each has its own .git and its own upstream.
# 877 MB of the 888 MB tree lives here. Track these as submodules or
# leave them out; do NOT commit them as plain files.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/work/
/TlsrComSwireWriter/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI-session scratch / handoff notes.
# These may contain private infrastructure details such as internal addresses,
# host labels, usernames, and local service endpoints. Keep them local unless
# they receive a fresh publication review.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AI_AUDIT_BRIEF.md
DEBUG_BRIEF.md
POSTMORTEM_*.md
REBUILD_NOTES.md
SOLVED.md

# AI-session analysis artifacts (regenerable scratch)
ota_verify/

# Local operational notes stay private.  Existing tracked legacy documents
# remain visible until deliberately removed from the index; this prevents a
# `.gitignore` rule from quietly disguising a public-history problem.
AI_BUGHUNT_BRIEF.md
AI_SWARM_PLAYBOOK.md
FIRMWARE_STATUS.md
HANDOFF.md
PI_SWIRE_SETUP.md
HANDOVER*.md
AI_*.md

# Bench-only analysis and capture helpers.  Keep reusable source tools such as
# dump/*.py trackable; these patterns intentionally cover only local runbooks,
# logs, and hardware-specific scripts.
dump/*_analysis*.md
dump/capture_*.sh
dump/flash_fixture_*.sh
dump/*.log

# Private hardware captures.  Do not use a global `*.bin` rule: source and
# deliberately distributable firmware artifacts may still need to be tracked.
dump/bench_*/
dump/dump_*.bin
dump/zt3l_MERGED.bin
dump/zt3l_MERGED.bin.sha256
dump/zt3l_full*.bin
dump/zt3l_full*.sha*
dump/*sram*.bin
dump/*nv*.bin
dump/*full*.bin
dump/private*/
tuya_plug_old.bin
tuya_plug_stock.bin

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local captures and operational handoffs are not public release material.
# See the narrow capture rules above; release/source firmware is intentionally
# not blanket-ignored.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

